  "recommendation": "Current action remains EA_ON. Reassess after the 12:30 UTC PPI/jobless-claims release and again through the 13:30 UTC cash open; upgrading to a higher Tail state requires observed persistent one-way structure, not the mere presence of the event.",
  "headline": "Futures are little changed pre-PPI as calm VIX and a contained Hormuz oil overhang offset scattered AI-hardware earnings misses",
  "body": "Nasdaq-100, S&P 500 and Dow futures were roughly flat to modestly higher in premarket trading after Wednesday's session lifted the Nasdaq 100 to a one-month high on megacap chipmaker strength. Overnight in Asia, NQ slipped after Cisco Systems' results underwhelmed; Cisco fell about 5.9% and Cerebras dropped roughly 17.4% in premarket trading with Coherent also lower, but this reads as company-specific AI-infrastructure earnings disappointment rather than confirmed broad breadth deterioration. The VIX is calm near 14.7, down about 4% on the day, and the 10-year Treasury yield eased slightly to roughly 4.68% ahead of the data. Brent crude remains below $90/bbl even as Iran's self-declared Strait of Hormuz authority claims persist; flows through the strait were reported near pre-war levels in the past week, so this is unresolved background risk rather than fresh transmission. Sufficiently granular current-session NQ bar-by-bar structure (pullback depth, failed-retracement count, extension after pullback) could not be independently verified at run time, so a persistent no-retracement trend can be neither confirmed nor ruled out. Tail stays low at 17%. Stress is elevated at 54% because the July PPI and initial jobless claims print at 12:30 UTC, followed by the U.S. cash open at 13:30 UTC, can produce a large intraday swing without by itself proving a pathological one-way price path.",
